                <pb facs="0367" n="361" xml:id="pg361"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-02-17"><hi rendition="#italic">February 17,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Conger reports the receipt on the 16th instant of an unsatisfactory edict
                    decreeing exile for Tuan and Lan without capital sentence, suicide for Chuang,
                    death for Yü Hsien, degradation and imprisonment for Chao Shu-chiao and Ying
                    Men, and undetermined punishment for Chi Hsiu and Hsü Cheng-yu.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
